> nethack is portable.

It does require write access to the file system.
In the programming language context of "portable", Nethack is fairly
portable, at least in terms of being a relatively standard C dialect,
but it requires one of a small selection of user interface platforms
in order to compile and run.

In the "portable" sense of being able to install and run it on a thumb
drive, I've done this on Windows, OSX and Linux.

I'd also suggest nethack.alt.org, for anyone with internet access.


